  "stem": "The function \\(f\\) is defined by \\(f(x) = 3^{x}\\). If \\(f(a) = 5\\), what is the value of \\(f(2a + 1)\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "75"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "\\(f(2a + 1) = 3^{2a + 1} = \\left(3^{a}\\right)^{2} \\cdot 3\\).",
    "Since \\(3^{a} = 5\\), \\(f(2a + 1) = 5^{2} \\cdot 3 = 75\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "a = log(5, 3)\nassert simplify(3**a) == 5\nassert simplify(3**(2*a + 1)) == 75 == Rational(spr_answers[0])",
